   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the insurance law, in relation to providing for the issuance\nof pet insurance",
    "basePrintNo": "S10225",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S10225-2025",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §1113, add §3463, Ins L",
    "lawSection": "Insurance Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S10225\n\nSPONSOR: BAILEY\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the insurance law, in relation to providing for the\nissuance of pet insurance\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThe purpose of this bill is to regulate and define the issuance of pet\ninsurance.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 -Amends subsection (a) to section 1113 of the insurance law to\nestablish in the definition of \"Animal insurance\" does not include pet\ninsurance.\n\nSection 2 - Subsection (a) amends the insurance law by adding a new\nsection 3462, which provides definitions including that of \"pet insur-\nance\" and related terms.\nSubsection (b) requires that the insurer shall use the definition of\nterms set forth by this section and make them available through a clear\nand conspicuous link on the main page of the insurers or insurer's\nprogram administrator's website. Provides that definitions shall not\nprohibit, or limit types of exclusions insurers may use in their poli-\ncies or requirements. Subsection (c) requires the disclosures pet insur-\ners must make to consumers. Subsection (d) clarifies that insurers have\nthe burden of proving preexisting condition exclusion applies to the\ncondition for which a claim is being made. Subsection (e) prohibits\ninsurers from marketing a wellness program as pet insurance.\nSubsection (f) prohibits an insurance producer from soliciting or nego-\ntiating a pet insurance product until after the producer is appropriate-\nly licensed and completed the require training identified in paragraph\nthree of this section.\nSubsection (g) directs promulgation of rules and regulations for imple-\nmentation to the superintendent.\nSubsection (h) establishes that all other applicable provisions of this\nsection of law shall apply to pet insurance except specific provisions\ngiven in this section.\n\nSection 3 - Establishes the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis bill seeks to establish a comprehensive regulatory framework for\nthe pet insurance industry in New York State. This act would create\nuniform definitions, offer better protection to owners, and generally\nreduce regulatory confusion. Several states, including California and\nMaine, have already adopted similar legislation.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2026: tabled\n\n2023-24: A8276 - tabled memo.39\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\nTo be determined.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect on the one hundred and eightieth day after it\nshall have become a law and shall apply to all policies entered,\nrenewed, modified or amended on or after such effective date. Effective\nimmediately, the addition, amendment and/or repeal of any rule or regu-\nlation necessary for the implementation of this act on its effective\ndate are authorized to be made and completed on or before such effective\ndate.\n",
